    metaDesc:'Three Ecuadorian regions host internationally connected communities with no international schooling: the tuna coast, the Amazon oil fields, and Cuenca\u2019s expatriate highlands.',
    intro:'Ecuador\u2019s international schooling sits in Quito and Guayaquil. Three of its most internationally connected communities do not. Manta runs one of the largest tuna processing complexes in the Americas. The Oriente — Coca, Lago Agrio, the Napo corridor — holds the oil fields that have funded much of the national economy for fifty years. And Cuenca hosts one of the largest North American expatriate populations in Latin America. None of the three has an international school. This article is about all of them.',
